## Configuration and deployment

The start and development scripts load `.env` when it exists, using Node.js's built-in environment
file support. Variables already set in the environment take precedence.
Do not commit `.env` files or secrets.
Set `NODE_ENV=production` when deploying; Express defaults to development otherwise.
<% if (options.git) { -%>
The generated `.gitignore` excludes `.env` files except `.env.example`.
<% } -%>
<% if (options.helmet) { -%>

Helmet adds security headers.
<% } -%>
<% if (options.compression) { -%>
Compression middleware compresses responses.
<% } -%>
<% if (options.cookies) { -%>
Cookie parsing makes cookies available as `req.cookies`.
<% } -%>
<% if (options.cors) { -%>

CORS allows any origin by default. Set `CORS_ORIGIN` to a comma-separated list of allowed origins.
<% if (webApi) { -%>
CORS applies to <%- options.corsScope === 'all' ? 'the whole app' : 'the API under `/api` only' %>.
<% } -%>
<% } -%>
<% if (options.rateLimit) { -%>

App routes allow 100 requests per client every 15 minutes by default; `/health` is never limited.
Set `RATE_LIMIT_MAX` and `RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS` to change these limits.
<% } -%>
<% if (trustProxy) { -%>

Behind a reverse proxy, set `TRUST_PROXY` to its addresses or the number of trusted proxy hops,
so the app sees the client's IP address and HTTPS protocol. Leave it unset without a trusted proxy.
<% } -%>
<% if (session) { -%>

Sessions are available as `req.session`. Set `SESSION_SECRET` to a long random secret:

```sh
node -e "console.log(crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
```

Production refuses to start without `SESSION_SECRET`. Session cookies use `SameSite=Lax` and are
`Secure` over HTTPS. The default in-memory store loses sessions on restart and is not suitable for
production; configure a persistent session store before deploying.
<% } -%>
<% if (csrf) { -%>

### CSRF tokens

Requests other than GET, HEAD and OPTIONS require the session's token or receive a 403 response.
Views receive `csrfToken`; forms send it in a hidden `_csrf` field, as the generated forms do.
JavaScript can read the `csrf-token` meta tag and send the token in an `x-csrf-token` header:

```js
const token = document.querySelector('meta[name="csrf-token"]').content;
await fetch('/users/new', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'x-csrf-token': token },
  body: new URLSearchParams({ name: 'Ada' })
});
```
<% if (webApi) { -%>

<% if (csrfSkipApi) { -%>
Routes under `/api` are excluded from CSRF protection. Do not authenticate them using the session
cookie; use another mechanism, such as a token in an Authorization header.
<% } else { -%>
Routes under `/api` also require the token for requests other than GET, HEAD and OPTIONS.
<% } -%>
<% } -%>
<% } -%>
<% if (uploads) { -%>

### File uploads

Files are saved in `uploads/` under random names and are not served as static files.
The default limit is 5 MB per file; set `UPLOAD_MAX_SIZE` in bytes to change it.
The allowed types are PDF, GIF, JPEG, PNG, WebP and plain text. Edit `TYPES` in
`routes/uploads.<%- ext %>` to change them. MIME types are supplied by clients, so verify file
contents before trusting them.
<% if (csrf) { -%>

Put the `_csrf` field before the file field, or send the token in an `x-csrf-token` header.
The upload route checks it before saving the file.
<% } -%>
<% } -%>
<% if (sass) { -%>

### Sass

Edit `public/stylesheets/style.scss`, not the compiled CSS. Start and development scripts compile
stylesheets before starting the server. Run `<%- command('css:watch') %>` in a second terminal
to recompile on change.

Sass is a development dependency. For a production-only install, compile stylesheets first with
`<%- command('css') %>` and start the server directly with
`node --env-file-if-exists=.env ./bin/www.<%- ext %>`.
<% } -%>
<% if (options.docker) { -%>

### Docker

Install dependencies first to create the lockfile, then build and run the production image:
<% if (session) { -%>
Set `SESSION_SECRET` in `.env` before running it.
<% } -%>

```sh
<%- pm %> install
docker build -t <%- name %> .
docker run <%- session ? '--env-file .env ' : '' %>-p 3000:3000 <%- name %>
```

The image runs as an unprivileged user with production dependencies, `NODE_ENV=production`,
a `/health` check and graceful shutdown. It does not copy `.env` files; pass environment variables
at runtime.
<% if (sass) { -%>
Stylesheets are compiled during the image build.
<% } -%>
<% if (uploads) { -%>
Mount a volume at `/app/uploads` to retain files when a container is replaced.
<% } -%>
<% } -%>
